# Build-context exclusions for the eden-service image.
#
# Dockerfile line 22 is `COPY --chown=eden:eden . .` -- it copies the WHOLE
# service directory into /app. Without this file that included every local
# .env.*, so real credentials (the dev Cosmos connection string, two Azure
# DevOps PATs) were baked into the image layer -- the same image tag prod
# builds, readable by anyone who can pull or `docker exec` it. Being
# gitignored does not help: .gitignore governs git, .dockerignore governs the
# build context, and these are separate mechanisms.
#
# Runtime env comes from compose `env_file:` / `--env-file`, never from a file
# inside the image, so nothing here is needed at run time. The load_dotenv()
# calls throughout source/ look for a bare `.env` in the working directory,
# which has never existed in this folder -- excluding these changes no
# behavior.
#
# Do NOT add: contracts/ (route_registry.json is loaded from /app/contracts
# at runtime -- see navigation_agent.py), source/, main.py, requirements.txt.

# ── Secrets: every env file, including .env.workitems and .env.template ──
.env
.env.*

# ── Git / VCS ──
.git
.gitignore

# ── Python build + cache artifacts ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── Local virtualenvs ──
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Docs and agent instructions: not read at runtime ──
docs/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# ── Local runtime output ──
logs/
*.log
